{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\n__author__ = 'MoonBall'\n\nimport sys\n# sys.stdin = open('data/D.in', 'r')\nT = 1\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef main():\n    P, K = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    # Special cases\n    if K == 0:\n        print(pow(P, P - 1, MOD))\n        return\n    if K == 1:\n        print(pow(P, P, MOD))\n        return\n\n    # Precompute the permutation\n    perm = [K * i % P for i in range(P)]\n    \n    # Track visited nodes and count cycles\n    seen = [False] * P\n    cycle_freq = [0] * P\n    res = 1\n\n    for i in range(P):\n        if seen[i]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Traverse the cycle\n        cycle_len = 0\n        j = i\n        while not seen[j]:\n            seen[j] = True\n            j = perm[j]\n            cycle_len += 1\n        \n        if cycle_len > 0:\n            cycle_freq[cycle_len] += 1\n\n    # Compute final answer\n    for L in range(2, P):\n        if cycle_freq[L]:\n            t = L * cycle_freq[L] + 1\n            res = (res * pow(t, cycle_freq[L], MOD)) % MOD\n\n    print(res)\n\nfor _ in range(T):\n    main()\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007;\n\nlong long modPow(long long base, long long exp, long long mod) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    base %= mod;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) {\n            result = (result * base) % mod;\n        }\n        base = (base * base) % mod;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n    long long P, K;\n    cin >> P >> K;\n    \n    // Special cases\n    if (K == 0) {\n        cout << modPow(P, P - 1, MOD) << endl;\n        return;\n    }\n    if (K == 1) {\n        cout << modPow(P, P, MOD) << endl;\n        return;\n    }\n\n    // Precompute the permutation\n    vector<long long> perm(P);\n    for (long long i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n        perm[i] = (K * i) % P;\n    }\n    \n    // Track visited nodes and count cycles\n    vector<bool> seen(P, false);\n    vector<long long> cycle_freq(P, 0);\n    long long res = 1;\n\n    for (long long i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n        if (seen[i]) {\n            continue;\n        }\n        \n        // Traverse the cycle\n        long long cycle_len = 0;\n        long long j = i;\n        while (!seen[j]) {\n            seen[j] = true;\n            j = perm[j];\n            cycle_len++;\n        }\n        \n        if (cycle_len > 0) {\n            cycle_freq[cycle_len]++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Compute final answer\n    for (long long L = 2; L < P; L++) {\n        if (cycle_freq[L]) {\n            long long t = L * cycle_freq[L] + 1;\n            res = (res * modPow(t, cycle_freq[L], MOD)) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << res << endl;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int T = 1;\n    for (int _ = 0; _ < T; _++) {\n        main();\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</co